<p class='content-paragraph'>
  By high school, I had no idea what I wanted to do with my life. Then a Turkish teacher showed me
  what it actually meant to read a book. Not for a grade. Seriously, with curiosity. I bought my
  first book: <em class='content-emphasis'>Think and Grow Rich</em>.
</p>

<p class='content-paragraph'>
  Something switched on inside me that year. It hasn’t switched off since.
</p>

<p class='content-paragraph'>
  <a href='https://www.youtube.com/@SamOvens' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>Sam Ovens</a
  > became my virtual mentor. His videos had a huge impact on me. I started reading everything I could
  find about sales, copywriting, and human psychology. Most teenagers weren’t reading books on copywriting.
  I had unlimited free time and a lot of questions.
</p>

