<p class='content-paragraph'>
  Then COVID hit. Stuck at home, I wanted to make something new. I love music, but I have a terrible
  voice, so I figured: why not make beats? My mom bought me FL Studio and a mini piano. I spent
  months learning it, intensely.
</p>

<BioGallery
  items={[
    {
      src: '/bio/fl-studio.jpg',
      alt: 'Making beats in FL Studio during lockdown',
    },
    { src: '/bio/piano.jpg', alt: 'The mini piano my mom bought me' },
  ]}
/>

<p class='content-paragraph'>
  Other things pulled me in, mostly marketing. I started an agency on my own: Facebook ads to bring
  leads to construction companies. I was studying economics at IAE Nancy at the same time. The
  agency failed. I passed my first year, then left. Sitting in a lecture hall for four or five hours
  bored me to death.
</p>

<p class='content-paragraph'>
  I spent the next year working at a very famous fast food chain. I was searching for myself. My
  girlfriend at the time supported me through it, and I’m grateful she did. I made a bit of money,
  and by pure chance, I found <a
    href='https://www.freecodecamp.org/'
    target='_blank'
    rel='noopener noreferrer'>freeCodeCamp</a
  >.
</p>

<p class='content-paragraph'>
  I learned HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, then followed <a
    href='https://www.udemy.com/course/the-web-developer-bootcamp/'
    target='_blank'
    rel='noopener noreferrer'>Colt Steele’s bootcamp</a
  >, which teaches you to build a CRUD app. My first real project was <a
    href='https://github.com/erenworld/campcalm'
    target='_blank'
    rel='noopener noreferrer'>CampCalm</a
  >. Then another one. Then another.
</p>

<p class='content-paragraph'>
  Beats and marketing had been fun, but this was different. Building something from zero, that
  didn’t exist the day before, excited me in a way nothing else had. I put the music aside and went
  all in.
</p>

<p class='content-paragraph'>
  The marketing years weren’t wasted, though. Everything I read about sales and psychology as a
  teenager is what I use today to sell myself, and my work.
</p>

<BioGallery items={[{ src: '/bio/first-code.jpg', alt: 'CampCalm, my first real project' }]} />

<p class='content-paragraph'>
  I joined <a href='https://www.epitech.eu/' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>Epitech</a> to
  go deeper. I learned C, then Python, then Rust. I’m now in my third year, with several internships behind
  me and more ahead. Next year, I’ll spend six months at
  <a href='https://www.itu.edu.tr/en' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'> ITU</a> in Istanbul,
  back in the country my parents left.
</p>

<BioGallery
  items={[
    { src: '/bio/epitech.jpg', alt: 'Epitech' },
    { src: '/bio/istanbul.jpg', alt: 'Istanbul, where I’ll study next year' },
